		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Bullet 2.24 released]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2363#p2363"><![CDATA[
Minor changes in the new Bullet 2.24 version:<br><br>- debugging for vehicle wheels (using the debugDrawer)<br>- improved vehicle demo (shifted the center of mass of the chassis for stability, other tweaks, still need lots of tuning before driving is fun)<br>- improved raytracer demo (can be used to visualize implicit collision shapes<br>- getUserPointer is a const method now<br><br>Download:<br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediawiki-1.5.8/index.php?title=Download" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediaw ... e=Download</a><br>Precompiled Win32 binary tech demos:<br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/index.php?dir=physics/&amp;file=Bullet-2.24-win32-demos.zip" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pu ... -demos.zip</a><br><br>Thanks for the feedback so far, and enjoy,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Thu Nov 09, 2006 5:01 am</p><hr />
